  "notes": "Las Positas College's own courses for the Plan (spec 24 → Data, college_courses). Code, title, units and C-ID are copied from the course pages of LPC's 2025-2026 catalog on laspositascollege.edu, the newest catalog LPC hosts itself. LPC's current catalog is on laspositas.curriqunet.com, which answers 403 to scripts, so nothing here was compared with it: a person checks each row against it. c_id is the first C-ID the course page prints without a condition; CHEM 1B and CHEM 12B print only a series C-ID (\"CHEM 120 S (if taken with CHEM 1A)\"), written here as CHEM 120S and CHEM 160S. Topics come from the C-ID number, the course title against the topic, or, for the TMC lists (comm-list-*, econ-list-*, polisci-*, psych-list-*, sociology-list-*, business-math, econ-calculus, math-list-a, diff-eq-and-linear-algebra), the list in LPC's own AA-T or AS-T page for that major in the same catalog (https://laspositascollege.edu/catalog/2025-2026/<subject>/<degree>-aa-t.php or -as-t.php). LPC has no CS AS-T. A course in an ADT list also gets the later list topics that say \"any List A course not already used\". The three rows with empty fields are course types the catalog doesn't settle; each says what to find. A second person checks each row against the catalog. Then run: npm run import -- data/raw/planning/college-courses-las-positas.json --dry-run",
